{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files -g '*governance-git-reads*' -g AGENTS.md -g '*backend-go*' -g '*documentation-style*'; rg -n 'func gitCommandContext|func TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator|not a git repository|gitCommandContext' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance* pose-mcp/internal/pose/git*; rg -n 'governance-git-reads-untranslated' .pose/specs .pose/knowledge .pose/results/delivery-validation.json\"","aggregated_output":"locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\nAGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/AGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go:647:\tcmd := gitCommandContext(ctx, append([]string{\"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", root}, args...)...)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go:358:var ErrGitUnavailable = errors.New(\"pose: not a git repository\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go:566:\treturn gitCommandContext(context.Background(), args...)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go:569:// gitCommandContext is gitCommand under ctx. Both read raw object history: a\npose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go:572:func gitCommandContext(ctx context.Context, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/git_locale_test.go:21:\t\t\"  echo 'fatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git' >&2\\n\" +\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go:228:\tcmd := gitCommandContext(ctx, append([]string{\"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", root}, args...)...)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/git_batch.go:36:\tcmd := gitCommandContext(ctx, \"-C\", r.root, \"cat-file\", \"--batch\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_git_untranslated_test.go:19:\tif strings.Contains(strings.ToLower(string(out)), \"not a git repository\") {\n.pose/results/delivery-validation.json:223:    \"pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\": \"sha256:5e40437148d8b70db856d97cec2c096282b5a03abaf5c9da858c8c9d5c0d1518\",\n.pose/results/delivery-validation.json:688:    \"pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\": \"sha256:355ba04f8c1ddc911e42ca1e861f2d57f85f84b224dcf70024ca7e4e9d4f1699\",\n.pose/results/delivery-validation.json:4285:      \"id\": \"pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\",\n.pose/results/delivery-validation.json:4288:      \"name\": \"governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\",\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:2:slug: pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:13:delivers: capability:governance-git-reads-untranslated\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:16:# Spec: pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:63:- capability:governance-git-reads-untranslated module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:65:Composto em produção por toda leitura de governança que roda Git (`pose check`, `pose index`, revisões). Check permanente `governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated|TestEveryGovernanceGitRunnerIsUntranslated|TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator' -count=1`.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md:124:- R1 [satisfied] test:TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated test:TestEveryGovernanceGitRunnerIsUntranslated check:governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; sed -n '540,610p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go; sed -n '560,730p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go; sed -n '180,320p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go; rg -n 'not a git repository|strings.Contains.*(stderr|Stderr)|LC_ALL|LANGUAGE' pose-mcp/internal --glob '*.go'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated.md; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; sed -n '540,610p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go; sed -n '560,730p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go; sed -n '180,320p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go; rg -n 'not a git repository|strings.Contains.*(stderr|Stderr)|LC_ALL|LANGUAGE' pose-mcp/internal --glob '*.go'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-15\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates: spec:pose-check-shares-the-federated-material@defect-fix\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:governance-git-reads-untranslated\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer o motor ler o stderr dos comandos Git de governança sem tradução, de modo que um diretório fora de qualquer repositório seja reconhecido como tal em qualquer locale.\n\n### Business value\nA checagem de paridade do espelho do Harness, que o harne8 roda também numa sessão `pt_BR.UTF-8`, reprovou com o pose-dist em `26b011d`: o teste `TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator`, da spec `pose-check-shares-the-federated-material`, acusou \"Git context could not be proved at the project root\". A descoberta de módulos classifica a falha de `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` procurando \"not a git repository\" no stderr, e em pt_BR o Git escreve a frase traduzida: um projeto fora de qualquer repositório ficava com o fechamento desconhecido. O motor já roda em `LC_ALL=C` os comandos cujo stderr ele lê fora da governança (`gitOutputUntranslated`, spec `pose-git-repository-detection-ignores-locale`); os comandos de governança não.\n\n### Constraints\n- Só o ambiente dos comandos Git de governança muda; a saída de plumbing que eles produzem não depende do locale.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Mudar os comandos Git fora da captura de governança.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: Every Git command the governance read view runs shall run with `LC_ALL=C` and `LANGUAGE=C`, so a failure classified by its stderr is classified the same way under any locale.\n\n### Non-functional\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Security\n- Nenhuma mudança.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Em `LC_ALL=C`, nada muda.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/governance_read_view_git.go` e `pose/governance_read_view_stream.go`: o ambiente comum dos dois executores dos comandos de governança, o que captura e o que transmite.\n\n### Artifacts\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_git_untranslated_test.go\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:governance-git-reads-untranslated module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por toda leitura de governança que roda Git (`pose check`, `pose index`, revisões). Check permanente `governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated|TestEveryGovernanceGitRunnerIsUntranslated|TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Nenhum: os comandos são de plumbing, e o ambiente de exec do Go usa o último valor de uma chave repetida.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] `LC_ALL=C` e `LANGUAGE=C` no executor de governança (R1).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste do coordenador rodado sob pt_BR, que reprova sem a mudança.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Context: a classificação lê o stderr em inglês.\n- Options considered: (a) reconhecer também a frase traduzida; (b) rodar os comandos de governança sem tradução.\n- Decision: (b).\n- Basis: R1\n- Rationale: (a) teria de conhecer cada tradução do Git; (b) é o mecanismo que o motor já adota para os outros comandos cujo stderr lê.\n- Consequences: todo stderr de Git que a governança classifica está em inglês.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nO teste do coordenador, sob `LC_ALL=pt_BR.UTF-8`, `LANGUAGE=pt_BR`; pulado onde o Git não está traduzido.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26, Git traduzido para pt_BR.\n- Notes: a paridade do espelho em pt_BR, rodada pelo harne8 com o pose-dist em 26b011d, reprovou só em `TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator`. Sem a mudança, `TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated` reprova com a mesma mensagem; com ela, passa.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: a governança classifica a falha do Git do mesmo jeito em pt_BR.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated test:TestEveryGovernanceGitRunnerIsUntranslated check:governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\n\n### Known gaps\n- O teste é pulado numa máquina sem a tradução do Git para pt_BR.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n### Review\n\nRodada 1 (run rrn-c5171f8ff89f3ebb, attestation rva-f215ab03914d85c5, changes-requested): 1 bloqueador, tratado. F1 o executor que transmite a saída do Git (`runGovernanceGitStreamContext`) não recebia o ambiente sem tradução: os dois executores passaram a usar o mesmo `governanceGitEnv`, e um teste com um `git` falso no PATH registra o locale de cada um sob uma sessão pt_BR; reprova com o executor de streaming antigo. Os outros executores de Git do motor (`snapshotGit`, `previewGit`, `gitCheckIgnore`) não classificam texto do stderr e ficam como estão. As ferramentas `artifact-check` e `surface-check` da rodada 1 saíram sem resultado porque o revisor usou um `pose` instalado no PATH, de outra revisão, que leu outro change set.\n\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n\t}\n\ttracked := map[string]bool{}\n\tif allowed != nil {\n\t\tout, err := snapshotGit(root, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-z\", \"--name-only\", commit)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, path := range bytes.Split(out, []byte{0}) {\n\t\t\ttracked[string(path)] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n\tresult := []string{}\n\tfor _, path := range changed {\n\t\t_, regularErr := dispatchRegularInputPath(root, path)\n\t\tif seen[path] || (allowed != nil && allowed(path, tracked[path]) && regularErr == nil) {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tseen[path] = true\n\t\tresult = append(result, path)\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(result)\n\treturn result, nil\n}\n\nfunc gitCommand(args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n\treturn gitCommandContext(context.Background(), args...)\n}\n\n// gitCommandContext is gitCommand under ctx. Both read raw object history: a\n// replace ref or a graft changes what a commit is, and every gate has to judge\n// the same commit (spec pose-history-readers-read-raw R1, D1).\nfunc gitCommandContext(ctx context.Context, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t// The graft file below is the null device, and Git hints at any graft file on\n\t// stderr, which a caller that reads stderr as uncertainty would take for a failure.\n\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"git\", append([]string{\"-c\", \"advice.graftFileDeprecated=false\"}, args...)...)\n\tenv := make([]string, 0, len(os.Environ())+2)\n\tfor _, kv := range os.Environ() {\n\t\tname, _, _ := strings.Cut(kv, \"=\")\n\t\tif !gitRedirectingEnv[name] {\n\t\t\tenv = append(env, kv)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tcmd.Env = append(env, \"GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1\", \"GIT_GRAFT_FILE=\"+os.DevNull)\n\treturn cmd\n}\n\nconst (\n\tgitEmptyTreeSHA1   = \"4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904\"\n\tgitEmptyTreeSHA256 = \"6ef19b41225c5369f1c104d45d8d85efa9b057b53b14b4b9b939dd74decc5321\"\n)\n\n// GitEmptyTree is the empty tree in commit's object format: the base of a change\n// set that starts at a repository's first commit (spec\n// pose-history-readers-read-raw R2, D2).\nfunc GitEmptyTree(commit string) string {\n\tif len(commit) == len(gitEmptyTreeSHA256) {\n\t\treturn gitEmptyTreeSHA256\n\t}\n\treturn gitEmptyTreeSHA1\n}\n\n// IsGitEmptyTree says that revision is the base of such a change set.\nfunc IsGitEmptyTree(revision string) bool {\n\treturn revision == gitEmptyTreeSHA1 || revision == gitEmptyTreeSHA256\n}\n\n// ChangeSetRange is the revision range of a change set for rev-list and log.\nfunc ChangeSetRange(base, head string) string {\n\tif IsGitEmptyTree(base) {\n\t\treturn head\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\ttype identity struct {\n\t\tRootDigest   string   `json:\"root_digest\"`\n\t\tArgsDigest   string   `json:\"args_digest\"`\n\t\tOutputLimit  int64    `json:\"output_limit\"`\n\t\tOutputDigest string   `json:\"output_digest\"`\n\t\tErrorDigest  string   `json:\"error_digest,omitempty\"`\n\t\tProducers    []string `json:\"producers\"`\n\t}\n\tstate.mu.Lock()\n\titems := make([]identity, 0, len(state.observations))\n\tfor _, item := range state.observations {\n\t\targs, _ := json.Marshal(item.args)\n\t\titems = append(items, identity{\n\t\t\tRootDigest: digestBytes([]byte(filepath.Clean(item.root))), ArgsDigest: digestBytes(args),\n\t\t\tOutputLimit:  item.maxOutputBytes,\n\t\t\tOutputDigest: digestBytes(append(append([]byte(nil), item.stdout...), item.stderr...)),\n\t\t\tErrorDigest:  errorDigest(item.errText), Producers: sortedBoolKeys(item.producers),\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tfor _, item := range state.streams {\n\t\targs, _ := json.Marshal(item.args)\n\t\titems = append(items, identity{\n\t\t\tRootDigest: digestBytes([]byte(filepath.Clean(item.root))), ArgsDigest: digestBytes(args),\n\t\t\tOutputLimit:  item.maxBytes,\n\t\t\tOutputDigest: \"streamed:\" + item.digest + \":\" + fmt.Sprint(item.length),\n\t\t\tErrorDigest:  errorDigest(item.errText), Producers: sortedBoolKeys(item.producers),\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tstate.mu.Unlock()\n\tsort.Slice(items, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\tif items[i].RootDigest != items[j].RootDigest {\n\t\t\treturn items[i].RootDigest < items[j].RootDigest\n\t\t}\n\t\tif items[i].ArgsDigest != items[j].ArgsDigest {\n\t\t\treturn items[i].ArgsDigest < items[j].ArgsDigest\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn items[i].OutputLimit < items[j].OutputLimit\n\t})\n\traw, _ := json.Marshal(items)\n\tsum := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\treturn \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(sum[:])\n}\n\nfunc runGovernanceGitCommand(files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64) ([]byte, error) {\n\tstdout, _, err := runGovernanceGitCommandOutput(files, root, args, limit)\n\treturn stdout, err\n}\n\nfunc runGovernanceGitCommandContext(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64) ([]byte, error) {\n\tstdout, _, err := runGovernanceGitCommandOutputContext(ctx, files, root, args, limit)\n\treturn stdout, err\n}\n\nfunc runGovernanceGitCommandOutput(files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64) ([]byte, []byte, error) {\n\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmitted(files, root, args, limit, nil)\n}\n\nfunc runGovernanceGitCommandOutputContext(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64) ([]byte, []byte, error) {\n\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext(ctx, files, root, args, limit, nil)\n}\n\n// runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmitted admits each stream chunk before the\n// bounded output buffer retains it. The operation callback is shared with\n// Files reads, so concurrent producers cannot spend the same remaining bytes.\nfunc runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmitted(files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool) ([]byte, []byte, error) {\n\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext(context.Background(), files, root, args, limit, admit)\n}\n\n// runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext admits each stream chunk before\n// the bounded output buffer retains it and executes Git under ctx.\n// governanceGitEnv is added to every Git command the governance read view\n// runs, captured or streamed. Governance classifies Git's failures by what\n// Git writes to stderr, so Git writes it untranslated: a translated \"not a\n// git repository\" left a directory outside any repository unknown under\n// pt_BR (spec pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated).\nvar governanceGitEnv = []string{\"GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\", \"LC_ALL=C\", \"LANGUAGE=C\"}\n\nfunc runGovernanceGitCommandOutputAdmittedContext(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool) ([]byte, []byte, error) {\n\tif limit < 0 {\n\t\treturn nil, nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tfiles = FilesOrNative(files)\n\tif ctx == nil {\n\t\tctx = context.Background()\n\t}\n\tcmd := gitCommandContext(ctx, append([]string{\"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", root}, args...)...)\n\tcmd.WaitDelay = 2 * time.Second\n\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, governanceGitEnv...)\n\toutput := &boundedGovernanceGitOutput{limit: limit, admit: admit}\n\tcmd.Stdout = governanceGitStream{output: output, stderr: false}\n\tcmd.Stderr = governanceGitStream{output: output, stderr: true}\n\terr := cmd.Run()\n\tstdout, stderr, exceeded := output.values()\n\tif exceeded {\n\t\treturn nil, nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif exit, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError); ok {\n\t\t\texit.Stderr = append([]byte(nil), stderr...)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn stdout, stderr, &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: err}\n\t}\n\tif len(stderr) > 0 {\n\t\tdetail := strings.TrimSpace(string(stderr))\n\t\tif detail == \"\" {\n\t\t\tdetail = \"Git wrote unclassified stderr output\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn stdout, stderr, &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: errors.New(detail)}\n\t}\n\treturn stdout, stderr, nil\n}\n\ntype boundedGovernanceGitOutput struct {\n\tmu       sync.Mutex\n\tlimit    int64\n\tused     int64\n\tadmit    func(int64) bool\n\tstdout   bytes.Buffer\n\tstderr   bytes.Buffer\n\texceeded bool\n}\n\ntype governanceGitStream struct {\n\toutput *boundedGovernanceGitOutput\n\tstderr bool\n}\n\nfunc (stream governanceGitStream) Write(data []byte) (int, error) {\n\toutput := stream.output\n\toutput.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer output.mu.Unlock()\n\tif output.exceeded || int64(len(data)) > output.limit-output.used {\n\t\toutput.exceeded = true\n\t\treturn 0, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tif output.admit != nil && !output.admit(int64(len(data))) {\n\t\toutput.exceeded = true\n\t\treturn 0, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tvar err error\n\tif stream.stderr {\n\t\t_, err = output.stderr.Write(data)\n\t} else {\n\t\t_, err = output.stdout.Write(data)\n\t}\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\toutput.used += int64(len(data))\n\t}\n\treturn len(data), err\n}\n\nfunc (output *boundedGovernanceGitOutput) values() ([]byte, []byte, bool) {\n\toutput.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer output.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn append([]byte(nil), output.stdout.Bytes()...), append([]byte(nil), output.stderr.Bytes()...), output.exceeded\n}\n\t// read is proven unchanged without it (review round 1, F1 and F3).\n\tfor _, item := range streams {\n\t\tauditContext := item.ctx\n\t\tcancel := func() {}\n\t\tif item.hasDeadline {\n\t\t\tauditContext, cancel = context.WithDeadline(auditContext, item.deadline)\n\t\t}\n\t\tdigest, length, _, err := governanceAuditGitStream(auditContext, item.files, item.root, item.args, item.maxBytes, admit, io.Discard)\n\t\tcancel()\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, errGovernanceReadViewBudget) {\n\t\t\tfor producer := range item.producers {\n\t\t\t\tresult.UnknownProducers[producer] = appendUnique(result.UnknownProducers[producer], \"Git streamed final audit exceeded its byte budget\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif digest != item.digest || length != item.length || streamErrorDigest(err) != item.errText {\n\t\t\tfor producer := range item.producers {\n\t\t\t\tresult.ChangedProducers[producer] = true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trootDigest := digestBytes([]byte(filepath.Clean(item.root)))\n\t\t\targsDigest := digestBytes([]byte(strings.Join(item.args, \"\\x00\")))\n\t\t\tresult.ChangedPaths = append(result.ChangedPaths, \"git:\"+strings.TrimPrefix(rootDigest, \"sha256:\")+\":\"+strings.TrimPrefix(argsDigest, \"sha256:\"))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// governanceStreamRun and governanceAuditGitStream run streamed reads during\n// the operation and in its final audit.\nvar (\n\tgovernanceStreamRun      = runGovernanceGitStreamContext\n\tgovernanceAuditGitStream = runGovernanceGitStreamContext\n)\n\n// runGovernanceGitStreamContext runs Git like the captured reads do and\n// writes its stdout to sink as it arrives, admitting each chunk before it is\n// written and hashing it; stderr is kept bounded. It returns the stdout's\n// digest and length. A non-empty stderr is an error, as for captured reads.\nfunc runGovernanceGitStreamContext(ctx context.Context, files Files, root string, args []string, limit int64, admit func(int64) bool, sink io.Writer) (string, int64, []byte, error) {\n\tif limit <= 0 {\n\t\treturn \"\", 0, nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\t_ = FilesOrNative(files)\n\tif ctx == nil {\n\t\tctx = context.Background()\n\t}\n\tif sink == nil {\n\t\tsink = io.Discard\n\t}\n\tcmd := gitCommandContext(ctx, append([]string{\"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", root}, args...)...)\n\tcmd.WaitDelay = 2 * time.Second\n\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, governanceGitEnv...)\n\tout := &governanceStreamWriter{limit: limit, admit: admit, sink: sink, hash: sha256.New()}\n\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = out\n\tcmd.Stderr = &limitedStderr{buf: &stderr, limit: governanceStreamStderrLimit}\n\terr := cmd.Run()\n\tif out.exceeded {\n\t\treturn \"\", 0, nil, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tdigest := \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(out.hash.Sum(nil))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif exit, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError); ok {\n\t\t\texit.Stderr = append([]byte(nil), stderr.Bytes()...)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn digest, out.written, stderr.Bytes(), &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: err}\n\t}\n\tif stderr.Len() > 0 {\n\t\tdetail := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\t\tif detail == \"\" {\n\t\t\tdetail = \"Git wrote unclassified stderr output\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn digest, out.written, stderr.Bytes(), &GitSnapshotError{Operation: strings.Join(args, \" \"), Cause: errors.New(detail)}\n\t}\n\treturn digest, out.written, nil, nil\n}\n\ntype governanceStreamWriter struct {\n\tmu       sync.Mutex\n\tlimit    int64\n\twritten  int64\n\tadmit    func(int64) bool\n\tsink     io.Writer\n\thash     hash.Hash\n\texceeded bool\n}\n\nfunc (w *governanceStreamWriter) Write(data []byte) (int, error) {\n\tw.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer w.mu.Unlock()\n\tif w.exceeded || int64(len(data)) > w.limit-w.written || w.admit != nil && !w.admit(int64(len(data))) {\n\t\tw.exceeded = true\n\t\treturn 0, errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tif _, err := w.sink.Write(data); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tw.hash.Write(data)\n\tw.written += int64(len(data))\n\treturn len(data), nil\n}\n\ntype limitedStderr struct {\n\tbuf   *bytes.Buffer\n\tlimit int\n}\n\nfunc (w *limitedStderr) Write(data []byte) (int, error) {\n\tif room := w.limit - w.buf.Len(); room > 0 {\n\t\tif len(data) > room {\n\t\t\tw.buf.Write(data[:room])\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tw.buf.Write(data)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn len(data), nil\n}\n\n// streamErrorDigest is the fixed-size identity of a streamed read's error.\nfunc streamErrorDigest(err error) string {\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn digestBytes([]byte(errorText(err)))\n}\npose-mcp/intern